{"name":"After Dark","hex":"#3c3535","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"after dark","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Prepositional phrase","definitions":["After nightfall; at night."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bookmaker's clerk.","A shark."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/after_dark"}],"entries":[{"title":"After Dark (Kitty Wells album)","blocks":[{"text":"After Dark is an album recorded by Kitty Wells and released in 1959 on the Decca label. On its release, Billboard praised the \"haunting nasal quality\" of her voice and called the album another \"great collection of ballads having to do with the seamy and sinful sides of life, sung as only Kitty Wells can sing them.\""}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/38/After_Dark_%28Kitty_Wells_album%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/After_Dark_(Kitty_Wells_album)"},{"title":"After Dark (Andy Gibb album)","blocks":[{"text":"After Dark is the third and final studio album by English singer-songwriter Andy Gibb, released in February 1980, by RSO Records. It features Gibb's last US Top 10 single \"Desire\", along with \"I Can't Help It\" and two Bee Gees numbers \"Rest Your Love on Me\" and \"Warm Ride\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f5/After_Dark_Andy_Gibb_album_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/After_Dark_(Andy_Gibb_album)"},{"title":"After Dark (TV programme)","blocks":[{"text":"After Dark was a British late-night live television discussion programme that was broadcast weekly on Channel 4 between 1987 and 1991, and which returned for specials between 1993 and 1997. It was later revived by the BBC for a single series, broadcast on BBC Four in 2003."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/After_Dark_11th_June_1988.jpg/330px-After_Dark_11th_June_1988.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/After_Dark_(TV_programme)"},{"title":"Darkness","blocks":[{"text":"Darkness is the condition resulting from a lack of illumination, or an absence of visible light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Creation_of_Light.png/330px-Creation_of_Light.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darkness"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/After_Dark_on_13_August_1988.jpg/500px-After_Dark_on_13_August_1988.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/After_Dark_on_13_August_1988.jpg/1280px-After_Dark_on_13_August_1988.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/After_Dark_on_13_August_1988.jpg/500px-After_Dark_on_13_August_1988.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Money\", 13 August 1988","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAfter_Dark_on_13_August_1988.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/After_Dark%2C_26_June_1987%2C_%22Killing_With_Care%22.jpg/500px-After_Dark%2C_26_June_1987%2C_%22Killing_With_Care%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/After_Dark%2C_26_June_1987%2C_%22Killing_With_Care%22.jpg/1280px-After_Dark%2C_26_June_1987%2C_%22Killing_With_Care%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/After_Dark%2C_26_June_1987%2C_%22Killing_With_Care%22.jpg/500px-After_Dark%2C_26_June_1987%2C_%22Killing_With_Care%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org